The constructs in the concretes
description: the same logical graph, spelled in a .yo file, in json5p, and as a directory
- >
  The logical graph has a handful of constructs, and each main concrete spells all of them (or falls
  back where it cannot). The yamlover file surface is the reference; the json5p brace surface quotes
  its pointer expressions and has no tags; the directory concrete spreads the node over the filesystem
  with the `.yo` overlays:
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Construct
    - 'In a `.yo` file'
      width: 2
    - 'In json5p'
    - 'In a directory'
      width: 2
  - - keyed entry
    - '`key: value`; the null key `~: value`; the numeric string key `''1'': value` (a plain `1:` is a parse error - a position is authored by order)'
    - '`key: value` (no null key - a LossyError)'
    - 'a file or subdirectory named `key`'
  - - keyless entry
    - '`- value`'
    - 'an array element'
    - 'an `itemNN` member granted its position by a `- *: itemNN` pointer in `body.yo`'
  - - scalar self-value
    - 'a bare scalar line among the entries'
    - '- (falls back to yamlover)'
    - 'the directory''s own scalar line in `body.yo`'
  - - mixture (keyed + keyless)
    - entries interleaved freely
    - '- (falls back)'
    - 'ordered members, then the keyed-only remainder'
  - - pointer
    - '`*: pets: 1` (unquoted)'
    - '`*'': pets: 1''` (quoted)'
    - 'a `key: *path` line in `body.yo`'
  - - bookmark
    - '`&: P: k` - on the value''s line or its own'
    - '`&'': P: k''` (quoted)'
    - 'a bookmark line in `body.yo`'
  - - schema attachment
    - 'the `!!<...>` tag'
    - '- (no tags: overlay only)'
    - '`.yo/meta.yo`'
- >
  The two text surfaces meet mid-file: a flow token written across several lines is the inline switch
  to json5p
  ([K&R](*::language:concretes:03-yamlover:00-yamlover_stream:00-yamlover_code:00-yamlover_structured)),
  and everything json5p cannot hold falls back
  to block yamlover, silently and losslessly. A file and a subdirectory are equivalent representations
  of one node; the full storage rules are the [concretes part](*::language:concretes).
